                        {
                          "id": "p-step-4",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
                            "text": "Refrigerated trailers must meet federal DOT regulations and any state-specific standards, depending on where you operate. In Florida, it's especially important to ensure your reefer trailer complies with safety requirements, proper weight distribution, lighting, and refrigeration capabilities, particularly when hauling perishable goods. If you're transporting food, you may also need to follow FDA guidelines under the Food Safety Modernization Act (FSMA), which requires temperature control monitoring and proper trailer sanitation.",
                            "align": "left",
                            "width": "full"
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "id": "p-step-4-2",
                          "type": "text",
                          "props": {
